# arXiv:2106.06463 — nougat extraction stub

**Paper:** Utkarsh Azad & Harjinder Singh, *"Quantum Chemistry Calculations
using Energy Derivatives on Quantum Computers"* (arXiv:2106.06463v1, 10 Jun 2021).

**Status:** Placeholder for parser stage. The replication in `report/`
worked directly from `work/paper.pdf` + `work/paper.txt` (plain-text
extraction sufficed for claim mining). A full nougat / marker MMD extraction
was not required to reach the REPLICATED verdict on the headline claim.

**Rationale:** QC-100 wave headline verification for this paper depended on
numerical reproduction (VQE energies, gradients, geometry-opt trajectory),
not on figure/equation OCR. The parser artifact is stubbed here rather than
regenerated to preserve compute budget (uicgpu is reserved for LUCID-100 OCR
per Rick's small-batch OCR allocation rule).

## To generate this artifact for real (future work)

Run on uicgpu when free (per small-batch OCR rule) or on Polaris (large-batch):
```
nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base --markdown
# or:
marker_single work/paper.pdf extraction/ --extract_images --paginate
```

Expected output: `extraction/nougat.mmd` containing full paper text with
equations (LaTeX-formatted), figures (Markdown image references), tables
(pipe-format), and section headers preserved.

